# Host crontab fragment for rpi-homeserver — generic jobs only, personal ones go in rpi-services.
#
# Not installed on its own: scripts/setup/install-crontab.sh merges both repos' fragments and
# apply.sh runs it on every deploy, so committing a change here applies it. Editing the live
# crontab with `crontab -e` is overwritten on the next deploy.
#
# Paths are written as @PROJECT_DIR@, which install-crontab.sh replaces with this machine's checkout.
# A `# when: <service>` line makes the job below it conditional on that compose service being active
# here (COMPOSE_PROFILES), and `# when: file <path>` on that file existing under the checkout, so a
# node that runs a subset of the stack does not get jobs for what it does not have.
#
# What each script does: docs/architecture.md, "The scripts". The media, zram and disk numbers, and
# the tracker read-then-act pair, used to be five lines here and are now the pi-metrics and
# tracker-control services, scraped instead of pushed.

# Self-heal net for the deploy. The webhook handles pushes; this restarts anything that died and
# covers pushes that arrived while the Pi or the tunnel was down.
*/30 * * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/deploy/apply.sh >> @PROJECT_DIR@/apply.log 2>&1

# Being retired, commented out on 2026-08-24. The script stays until it is decided whether anything
# replaces it; see PENDING.md. 05:00 and not 02:00 was because Plex holds 02:00-05:00 for its own
# maintenance and both land on the same platters (docs/lifecycle.md).
#0 5 * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/ops/cutoff-search.sh >> @PROJECT_DIR@/cutoff-search.log 2>&1

0 4 * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/ops/backup.sh >> @PROJECT_DIR@/backup.log 2>&1

# Bazarr keeps the subtitle tracks of a file Radarr has already replaced, and a language it wrongly
# believes is embedded is never searched for. Its own 04:00 index only inserts, so this runs after
# it and takes the rows away. 05:40 and not inside apply.sh because a full pass is ~55s of ffprobe
# over every media file, and Plex holds 02:00-05:00 on the same platters (docs/lifecycle.md).
# when: bazarr
40 5 * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/sync/bazarr-prune-subs.py >> @PROJECT_DIR@/bazarr-prune-subs.log 2>&1

# Dead man's switch, so someone outside notices within minutes if the Pi goes dark. No-op unless
# HEALTHCHECK_URL is set. See docs/alerting.md.
* * * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/ops/heartbeat.sh

# A minute is Oracle's own measured rate: exactly one launch call gets through per ~60s however
# hard you ask, so anything faster only raises the refusal count. Exits for good once the instance
# exists, so this is safe to leave forever. One summary line an hour, not one per run.
# when: file appdata/oci/api_key.pem
* * * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/ops/oci-hunt.py >> @PROJECT_DIR@/oci-hunt.log 2>&1

# Prowlarr backs a failed indexer off for up to 24h, so an hour of the ISP blocking a site would
# otherwise cost a day of it being unusable. Probes the site first, never searches.
# when: prowlarr
8,23,38,53 * * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/ops/indexer-retry.py >> @PROJECT_DIR@/indexer-retry.log 2>&1

# 05:00, after Plex's 02:00-05:00 maintenance on the same platters, the one-pace build at 03:00 and the 04:00 backup.
# One file after another until 07:00, about ten minutes each, nice and ionice. Leaves anything still hardlinked
# alone, so it never drops a link qbit-manage would read as noHL. Which codecs it converts comes
# from what pi-metrics saw a server refuse for a client: appdata/pi-metrics/audio-recodes.json.
# Shares a lock with services/audio-convert, and waits for a conversion started from that page.
# when: audio-convert
0 5 * * * @PROJECT_DIR@/scripts/sync/audio-compat.py >> @PROJECT_DIR@/audio-compat.log 2>&1
